<title>USA: Cytec proposes up to 115 job cuts at plant.</title>
<headline>Cytec proposes up to 115 job cuts at plant.</headline>
<dateline>WEST PATERSON, N.J. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cytec Industries Inc said on Friday that its Netherlands subsidiary proposed a restructuring that could cut up to 115 jobs to the Works Council and unions at its Botlek plant.</p>
<p>The proposal is subject to negotiations with the Works Council and unions at the plant that employs 360, Cytec said.</p>
<p>Features of the plan include a revamping of its organization, relocation of certain manufacturing to other Cytec sites, a potential investment in the polymers additives business and the job cuts over a two-year period, Cytec said.</p>
</text>
